      "name": null,
      "problem": "If there are $21$ pears and $15$ apples, then what number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of pears to apples is $7:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $7$ pears for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ apples.",
      "worked_solution": "Since there are $21$ pears and $15$ apples, the ratio of pears to apples is $21:15.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,21 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,15 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,7 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $21:15$ is equivalent to $7:5.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is \"The ratio of pears to apples is $7:5\\,$ because there are $7$ pears for every $5\\,$ apples.\"\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $5.$",
